  "Question": "What time was it \\(2011\\) minutes after the beginning of January \\(1,\\) \\(2011?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "January \\(1\\) at \\(9:31\\) PM",
    "B": "January \\(1\\) at \\(11:51\\) PM",
    "C": "January \\(2\\) at \\(3:11\\) AM",
    "D": "January \\(2\\) at \\(9:31\\) AM",
    "E": "January \\(2\\) at \\(6:01\\) PM"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The beginning of January \\(1\\) is midnight. One full day contains \\(24\\times60=1440\\) minutes, leaving\n\\[\n2011-1440=571\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nSince \\(571=9\\times60+31\\), the remaining time is \\(9\\) hours and \\(31\\) minutes. One day after the starting time is midnight on January \\(2\\), so the requested time is January \\(2\\) at \\(9{:}31\\) AM, choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
